# Reflection Beam-1.0-501B-A23B NVFP4, arm a2: TWO DGX Station GB300s, SGLang TP2 over one 400G RoCE link (nnodes 2), no weight offload,
# DFlash2 speculative decoding (reflection/Beam-1.0-501B-A23B-DFlash2, --speculative-dflash-block-size 8; the drafter's config.json says 16).
# Run 2026-10-16 19:03-19:27 PT (the third arm of one window that started 17:50 PT with a1 and b1; boot 1, 0 retries).
# Excerpt: lines selected verbatim from the raw files named below; host names, GPU UUIDs, rail IPs and private paths replaced with
# <placeholders>. Times are Pacific (PT).
# Definitions: decode_agg = C x 1000 / mean TPOT (tok/s, the repo's decode metric; TPOT = (t_last - t_first) / (completion tokens - 1)
# per request, so it excludes TTFT and queueing); output_tok_s = all completion tokens / wall-clock of the run, including TTFT. decode_agg is
# NOT user-seen throughput; output_tok_s is closer to it. Real text = public CNN/DailyMail 3.0.0 test articles, the long pool of
# recipes/kimi-k3/bench/build_pool_k3.py (slices eval-c1-r1..r3: first prompt each; eval-c16: first 4 / 16 prompts), about 8,230-8,370 Beam
# prompt tokens, chat template with reasoning_effort minimal, 512 forced output tokens (ignore_eos + min_tokens), temperature 0, streaming
# (bench/kbench_chat_beam.py). Each run has its own nonce prefix and a separate warm-up slice. SGLang exposes no prefix-cache hit/query
# counters, so prefix_hit_pct / prefix_queries read 0 by construction; hygiene is the nonce + disjoint slices, and the server's
# cache_hit_rate gauge (recorded) read 0.0. chunk_acc = completion tokens / streamed chunks = observed tokens per verify step (1.0 without
# a drafter). catid = RANDOM TOKEN IDS (8,192 in / 1,024 forced out, temperature 0, one request, a fresh seed per rep; bench/beam_rand.py):
# a control, not real-text speed; the drafter accepts nothing on random ids (chunk_acc ~1.0). In rt-summary lines, spec_drafts /
# spec_draft_tokens / spec_accepted / acceptance_len are vLLM counters that SGLang does not expose (0 / null); chunk_acc and
# sglang_accept_len_gauge are the acceptance readings here.
# Engine: lmsysorg/sglang:beam, image id sha256:0ea912aadc3d7827858de9aa5a312c4d51c254e7dbe670dbbe8181895b92071d (its SGLang source
# matches sgl-project/sglang PR #44747 head f7473673 for the Beam model, offloader and argument files). Context 131072, BF16 KV, 16 running
# requests, chunked prefill 8192, page 64, trtllm_mha attention. All runs on stock SGLang (no patches, no hooks).

--- boot-a2/try1/launch-rank0.txt
